# Corpus unit sapg/C06 — gap (unmet-mandatory-CQ path: variance reporting)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/sapg.yaml C06 (causal, dose_response; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline:
# entropy regularization of the follower policies improves performance on harder exploration
# tasks — sigma=0.005 improves Reorientation by up to 16.5% over sigma=0, while sigma=0 is
# optimal on the easier AllegroHand, Regrasping, and Throw; a three-level sweep
# sigma in {0, 0.003, 0.005} on all tasks with a sigma=0 baseline (E04 / E06, Figure 6).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * dose_response maps to component_ablation (3-level coefficient sweep with a sigma=0
#     no-treatment baseline). Task-conditional claim; binding conjunct is the positive effect on
#     the hard task Reorientation: contributes(follower_entropy_reg, sapg, reorientation_performance).
#     The null/negative effect on the easy tasks is the scope qualifier, kept in nl and refs.
#   * The mandatory variance_reported CQ is unmet, so no complete component_ablation is
#     declarable (E2-style gap). Annotation CQ "is seed-level variance reported so the 16.5%
#     effect is distinguishable from noise?" is mandatory unmet-gap — E06 specifies 5 seeds but
#     Procedure step 2 asks only to "report final performance and learning curves", with no
#     stderr (unlike E02). This is the corpus's most systematic gap (M0 summary section 2).
#   * single_variable and protocol_parity ARE met: annotation CQ (only sigma varies, all other
#     SAPG settings held fixed) and CQ (sigma=0 baseline present on every task). The optional
#     mechanism CQ (entropy -> exploration tested beyond correlation with task difficulty) is
#     unmet-gap and omitted (optional, no status effect).
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact sapg at sha256:f4108aa329a9
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar ---------------

claim c06
  nl      = "Follower entropy regularization (sigma=0.005) improves SAPG on the harder exploration task Reorientation by up to 16.5 percent over sigma=0, while sigma=0 is optimal on the easier AllegroHand, Regrasping, and Throw; only sigma varies across {{0, 0.003, 0.005}} with a sigma=0 baseline on every task, but no per-seed variance is reported"
  formal  = contributes(follower_entropy_reg, sapg, reorientation_performance)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the E06 per-(sigma, task) sweep cells (Reorientation up to +16.5% at
# sigma=0.005, Figure 6), folded into refs per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e06, ablation_effect(follower_entropy_reg, sapg, reorientation_performance, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C06, logic/experiments.md#E06, Figure-6, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

leaf e2 : isolated(follower_entropy_reg, e06)
